														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4096796">
									

<p>I really love how nonplussed the Foundation is regarding sapiemt darkmatter, so much so that it's not even anomalous by their standards.</p>
<p>I wish that this stayed focused on interactions between DMIs, primarily due to how the speech was handled: it's not perfect, but it sufficiently captures the portrayal of an alien intelligence much better than is typically seen, though a large part of this is lost in the assertations, where it veers away from approximated translations as can be understood by humans and into direct dialogue - a weakness I'm willing to overlook only because the technical writing was otherwise sound.</p>
<p>To nitpick, it seems odd that it would use the term 'Higgs field' I would think that it has its own frame of reference for that &#8212; not something tied to our naming conventions.</p>

							</div>

								
					
